{"recall":{"defs":[["Encoder–decoder","Read input into context, generate output from it."],["Context bottleneck","All input squeezed into one fixed vector."],["Attention","Weighted sum of values with softmax(query–key scores)."],["Query / key / value","What we seek / what we match / what we retrieve."],["Scaled dot-product","softmax(QKᵀ/√d_k)V."],["Additive attention","vᵀtanh(W_q q + W_k k)."],["Self / cross attention","Q, K, V from one sequence / Q from one, K, V from another."],["Causal mask","−∞ on future positions."],["Positional encoding","Position signal added to embeddings."]],"formulas":["\\alpha_i=\\frac{\\exp(\\text{score}(\\mathbf q,\\mathbf k_i))}{\\sum_j\\exp(\\text{score}(\\mathbf q,\\mathbf k_j))},\\ \\ \\mathbf c=\\sum_i\\alpha_i\\mathbf v_i","\\text{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\\mathrm{softmax}(QK^T/\\sqrt{d_k})V","e_{t,i}=\\mathbf v^T\\tanh(W_ss_{t-1}+W_hh_i)","\\text{MultiHead}=\\text{Concat}(\\text{head}_1..\\text{head}_h)W_O","PE(pos,2i)=\\sin(pos/10000^{2i/d}),\\ PE(pos,2i+1)=\\cos(pos/10000^{2i/d})","\\mathrm{Var}(\\mathbf q^T\\mathbf k)=d_k"],"takeaways":["Attention removes the fixed-context bottleneck.","Soft, differentiable lookup: scores → softmax → weighted values.","Scale dot products by √d_k.","Self, cross, masked and multi-head variants.","Add positional encodings: attention is order-blind."],"confused":[["Self- vs cross-attention","Same sequence vs two sequences."],["Bahdanau vs Luong","Additive with s_{t−1} vs multiplicative/dot with s_t."],["Teacher forcing vs free running","Ground-truth vs own previous outputs."],["Invariant vs equivariant","Unchanged vs reordered with the input."],["Learned vs sinusoidal positions","Parameters per position vs fixed formula that extrapolates."]],"minute":"Encoder–decoder RNNs compress the input into one context vector, which fails on long inputs. Attention keeps all encoder states and builds a new context at each decoder step: scores e_i = score(q, k_i), weights α = softmax(e), context c = Σ α_i v_i. Scores can be dot products (fast), scaled dot products qᵀk/√d_k (the Transformer default, because Var(qᵀk) = d_k), additive vᵀtanh(W_q q + W_k k) as in Bahdanau's 2014 translation model, or multiplicative qᵀWk. Self-attention uses Q, K, V from one sequence, cross-attention queries another sequence, causal masks add −∞ to future positions for generation, and multi-head attention concatenates h heads and projects with W_O. Self-attention has O(1) path length and full parallelism at O(n²d) cost, but is permutation-equivariant, so positional encodings (learned or sinusoidal, where PE(pos + k) is a rotation of PE(pos)) are added."},"flashcards":[["Why encoder–decoder?","Input and output lengths differ (T ≠ T′)"],["Encoder context","$\\mathbf c=h_T^{enc}$"],["Exposure bias","Trained on ground truth, tested on own predictions"],["Context bottleneck problems","Information loss, fixed capacity, uniform encoding"],["Attention output","$\\sum_i\\alpha_i\\mathbf v_i$ with $\\alpha=\\mathrm{softmax}(\\text{scores})$"],["Gold-price example context","≈ ₹6,261"],["Query / keys / values","What we seek / what we match / what we retrieve"],["Attention pooling of (3, 7, 2, 5) with (0.1, 0.5, 0.2, 0.2)","5.2 (max 7, average 4.25)"],["Dot-product example weights (correct)","(0.276, 0.484, 0.240) for scores (0.58, 1.14, 0.44)"],["Scaled dot-product attention","$\\mathrm{softmax}(QK^T/\\sqrt{d_k})V$"],["Additive (Bahdanau) score","$\\mathbf v^T\\tanh(W_q\\mathbf q+W_k\\mathbf k)$"],["Luong multiplicative score","$\\mathbf q^TW\\mathbf k$"],["Bahdanau context","$\\mathbf c_t=\\sum_i\\alpha_{t,i}h_i$, $\\alpha$ from $s_{t-1}$ and $h_i$"],["Causal mask","0 if j ≤ i, −∞ if j > i"],["Multi-head typical sizes","h = 8, d_model = 512, d_k = d_v = 64"],["Self-attention complexity / path length","$O(n^2d)$ / $O(1)$"],["Sinusoidal PE","$\\sin(pos/10000^{2i/d})$, $\\cos(\\cdot)$"],["Why sinusoids","PE(pos + k) = M_k · PE(pos): relative positions are linear"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["why","h1","h2",